Karol G Invites ‘Everyone To Be A Little More Dramatic, A Little More Extra’ With New Album ‘No Me Arrepiento de Sentir&nbsp;Tanto’

On the tracklist revealed Wednesday (Aug. 5), the artist surprised fans with star-studded collaborators Drake on “Ahí,” Bruno Mars on “Still” and Judeline and Rusowsky on “Bby Wow.” The 14-track set is also home to the previously released singles “Después de Ti” with Cigarettes After Sex guitarist Greg Gonzalez and “Matadora,&#8221; which debuted at No. 3 on the&nbsp; Billboard &nbsp;Hot Latin Songs chart on the tally dated Aug. 8, 2026.&nbsp;

Karol premiered the former during her first headlining weekend at Coachella in April, and the latter during the kickoff of her Viajando Por El Mundo Tropitour on July 24 in Chicago’s Soldier Field.

A follow-up to her 2025 Tropicoqueta album that debuted at No. 1 on Top Latin Albums and No. 3 on the all-genre Billboard 200 , No Me Arrepiento de Sentir Tanto (which translates to &#8220;I Don’t Regret Feeling So Much&#8221;), moves away from the prior vibrant and tropical-leaning album, and demonstrates a more intimate, stripped-down look at the artist born Carolina Giraldo Navarro.&nbsp;

“In my room, I have a ritual: I put up little lights, I burn candles and incense. I want people to listen to this new album that’s coming, in their own rooms, and see what comes up for them,” she said in an interview with Elle in which she discussed her new album. “I’d rather suffer because I lived too much — because I loved too much, because I had too much fun — than to not have had those experiences, you know? I’m inviting everyone to be a little more dramatic, a little more extra.”

The “Bichota” singer teased a new album was dropping during her concert at Rogers Stadium in Toronto on July 29.&nbsp;“I’ve been working on a project for a couple of months,” she told onlookers. “I’ve been locked in for months making new music. For months, I’ve been preparing a segment that will form part of this tour.”

